            <ArticleTitle>Interpretation of Quantitative Structure-Activity Relationship Models: Past, Present, and Future.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2618-2639</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.jcim.7b00274</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper is an overview of the most significant and impactful interpretation approaches of quantitative structure-activity relationship (QSAR) models, their development, and application. The evolution of the interpretation paradigm from &quot;model → descriptors → (structure)&quot; to &quot;model → structure&quot; is indicated. The latter makes all models interpretable regardless of machine learning methods or descriptors used for modeling. This opens wide prospects for application of corresponding interpretation approaches to retrieve structure-property relationships captured by any models. Issues of separate approaches are discussed as well as general issues and prospects of QSAR model interpretation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
